  "modeling_notes": [
    "The direct 2026-2027 Computer Science B.S. page is the canonical standard path. The separately published Cybersecurity and Data Science concentration pages remain explicit alternate requirement sets and are not silently made mandatory.",
    "The minimum standard major arithmetic is 25 math/science + 37 computer-science core + 15 additional upper-division = 77 credits; the published maximum is 80.",
    "The Liberal Arts Core introduction says 48-49 credits while the page's component footer says 48-50. The canonical actual-course path is 48 credits because the four-credit MTH 2040 major requirement is explicitly marked as satisfying the six-hour Quantitative Reasoning gate.",
    "The canonical standard major supplies 15 actual Core credits: MTH 2040 (4), required laboratory science (8), and SWE 1790 in Studies of Self (3). The remaining distinct Core coursework is therefore 33 credits, leaving ten credits to reach 120.",
    "A Liberal Arts Core course may not satisfy more than one listed Core area. The remaining contextual coursework must total eighteen credits after SWE 1790 and must include Community, Nation, and World coverage plus the Humanities/Fine Arts, Social/Behavioral Science, and Inclusive Excellence gates.",
    "The catalog lists one- and three-credit First-Year Experience possibilities but names SEM 1010 as the current three-credit course; SEM 1010 is canonical. Accelerated language and composition routes are preserved as alternates, not prospective schedules.",
    "The comprehensive examination, one Experiential Learning Activity, and cultural-activity attendance are zero-credit completion gates and remain explicit rather than being converted into elective credits."
  ],
